# Space Invaders, in Intent v0.6.0.
#   ./intent build gemini-build/build-09-invaders/invaders.intent -o build/invaders && build/invaders
# Left/right move the ship, space fires, q quits, enter plays again.
#
# Design note: Intent 0.6 cannot compare a record of one collection with a record of
# another collection ("a condition can look into one other collection in this version",
# and the other collection may only be compared with numbers, text and single values).
# So the player's shot is a pair of SINGLE VALUES (shot x, shot y), not a collection.
# Aliens and bombs are collections; each is only ever compared against single values.

The board is 32 wide and 16 high.

The ship starts at 16.
The score starts at 0.
The best starts at 0.
The lives start at 3.
The wave starts at 1.
The march starts at 1.
The descend starts at 0.
The hit starts at 0.
The respawn starts at 0.
The hurt starts at 0.

# The shot: a y of 0 means there is no shot in the air.
The shot x starts at 0.
The shot y starts at 0.

Aliens is a collection where each alien has an x (number), a y (number) and a kind (number).
Bombs is a collection where each bomb has an x (number) and a y (number).

Start with an alien at x 4, y 2, kind 1.
Start with an alien at x 8, y 2, kind 1.
Start with an alien at x 12, y 2, kind 1.
Start with an alien at x 16, y 2, kind 1.
Start with an alien at x 20, y 2, kind 1.
Start with an alien at x 4, y 4, kind 2.
Start with an alien at x 8, y 4, kind 2.
Start with an alien at x 12, y 4, kind 2.
Start with an alien at x 16, y 4, kind 2.
Start with an alien at x 20, y 4, kind 2.

# --- the ship
When the left key is pressed, the ship decreases by 1 if the ship is over 1.
When the right key is pressed, the ship increases by 1 if the ship is under 32.
When space is pressed, if the shot y is 0, the shot x becomes the ship.
When space is pressed, if the shot y is 0, the shot y becomes 15.

# --- the shot flies up; reaching the top it is gone
Every 50 milliseconds, the shot y decreases by 1 if the shot y is over 0.

# --- a shot meets an alien: note the hit, score it, take the alien away, spend the shot
Every 50 milliseconds, if any alien has an x equal to the shot x and a y equal to the shot y, the hit becomes 1.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the hit is 1, the score increases by 10 times the wave.
Every 50 milliseconds, remove the aliens whose x is the shot x and whose y is the shot y.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the hit is 1, the shot y becomes 0.
Every 50 milliseconds, if the hit is 1, the hit becomes 0.

# --- the fleet marches; at an edge it turns and steps down
Every 400 milliseconds, the x of each alien increases by the march.
Every 400 milliseconds, if any alien has an x over 31, the descend becomes 1.
Every 400 milliseconds, if any alien has an x under 2, the descend becomes 1.
Every 400 milliseconds, if the descend is 1, the march becomes 0 minus the march.
Every 400 milliseconds, if the descend is 1, increase the y of every alien by 1.
Every 400 milliseconds, if the descend is 1, the descend becomes 0.

# --- bombs fall from random columns; more of them in later waves
Every 900 milliseconds, add a bomb whose x is a random number between 1 and 32 and whose y is 6.
Every 900 milliseconds, if the wave is over 2, add a bomb whose x is the ship and whose y is 3.
Every 150 milliseconds, the y of each bomb increases by 1.
Every 150 milliseconds, if any bomb has an x equal to the ship and a y equal to 16, the hurt becomes 1.
Every 150 milliseconds, if the hurt is 1, the lives decrease by 1.
# (Bug found: "if the hurt is 1, remove the bombs whose y is at least 14" is refused;
#  the same condition written AFTER the where-clause is accepted.)
Every 150 milliseconds, remove the bombs whose y is at least 14 if the hurt is 1.
Every 150 milliseconds, if the hurt is 1, the hurt becomes 0.
Every 150 milliseconds, remove the bombs whose y is over 16.

# --- a cleared fleet brings the next, faster-scoring wave
Every 100 milliseconds, if no alien has a y over 0, the respawn becomes 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, the wave increases by 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, add an alien whose x is 4, whose y is 2 and whose kind is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, add an alien whose x is 10, whose y is 2 and whose kind is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, add an alien whose x is 16, whose y is 2 and whose kind is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, add an alien whose x is 22, whose y is 2 and whose kind is 1.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, add an alien whose x is 7, whose y is 4 and whose kind is 2.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, add an alien whose x is 13, whose y is 4 and whose kind is 2.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, add an alien whose x is 19, whose y is 4 and whose kind is 2.
Every 100 milliseconds, if the respawn is 1, the respawn becomes 0.

# --- standing rules
When the score is over the best, the best becomes the score.

The game is over when the lives are under 1.
The game is over when any alien has a y over 14.

# --- what you see (later drawings cover earlier ones)
Draw each bomb at its x and y as a red "!".
Draw each alien whose kind is 1 at its x and y as a magenta "W".
Draw each alien whose kind is 2 at its x and y as a cyan "M".
Draw a yellow "|" at the shot x and the shot y.
Draw a green "A" at the ship and 16.
Show the score, the best, the lives and the wave above the board.
